  "narrative": "The feedback path is weakest (most negative) for the tightly sealed earmolds and strongest for the open dome, consistent with the amount of sound leaking back to the hearing-aid microphone. Inserting the measurement probe slightly increases the feedback path for loosely sealed couplings, because the additional slit forms a leak. This is the physical mechanism behind reduced usable gain in real-ear measurements, and it is reported here rather than hidden.",
